# Flag 3 – Runtime Function Resolution Tampering

## Invariant
Runtime function resolution must bind only trusted and expected
implementations.

## Telemetry
No telemetry exists to verify runtime symbol resolution or function
pointer integrity. The assessment evaluates this lack of verification.

## Observation
Observed. Function resolution occurs without validation, allowing
tampered or redirected bindings to execute unnoticed.

## Security Impact
Tampered function resolution enables malicious logic execution
without altering visible control flow or output.

## Limitations
Dynamic loader behavior is inferred through design analysis rather
than active instrumentation.

